WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:44.087
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:44.357 --> 00:48.069
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

3
00:49.445 --> 00:53.324
‎Martial law troops ‎have cleared out the remaining rioters.

4
00:53.908 --> 00:55.535
‎The riot has been suppressed.

5
00:56.035 --> 01:00.248
‎Drop your weapons ‎and surrender now to survive,

6
01:00.331 --> 01:01.499
‎or face execution.

7
01:02.292 --> 01:03.585
‎We repeat.

8
01:03.668 --> 01:05.920
‎The rioters have been put down.

9
01:06.004 --> 01:07.755
‎Drop your weapons and surrender.

10
01:07.839 --> 01:10.049
‎Anyone who resists will be shot on sight.

11
02:38.346 --> 02:43.268
‎JI DU-SEOK

12
02:43.351 --> 02:47.814
‎PATIENT: JI DU-SEOK ‎PRIMARY: KIM HYEON-MIN

13
02:52.026 --> 02:54.946
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

14
02:55.530 --> 02:57.615
‎EPISODE 7

15
03:05.456 --> 03:06.833
‎-No! ‎-Mr. Oh!

16
03:21.347 --> 03:23.016
‎Rough night, huh?

17
03:24.017 --> 03:25.268
‎Did you see?

18
03:25.351 --> 03:26.811
‎-See what? ‎-That man.

19
03:27.729 --> 03:28.563
‎Why do you ask?

20
03:28.646 --> 03:30.690
‎Because I'm curious!

21
03:30.773 --> 03:32.692
‎I heard he aged a lot in a short while.

22
03:32.775 --> 03:33.985
‎Myocardial infarction, right?

23
03:34.485 --> 03:37.238
‎Human life is so unpredictable.

24
03:37.905 --> 03:40.408
‎Just last year, ‎he was on a golf course saying,

25
03:40.491 --> 03:42.243
‎"History will judge that!"

26
03:42.327 --> 03:44.037
‎Then he took off in a golf cart.

27
03:44.620 --> 03:45.830
‎-I'm heading in. ‎-Hey.

28
03:46.789 --> 03:49.667
‎Did Mr. Oh Sang-beom do that ‎knowing he'd be here?

29
03:49.751 --> 03:50.793
‎After seeing the news?

30
03:50.877 --> 03:51.711
‎No.

31
03:53.254 --> 03:55.506
‎Do you want me to go? ‎I can find someone else.

32
03:55.590 --> 03:57.342
‎Okay, okay, I'll stop.

33
03:57.425 --> 04:00.011
‎I was just talking ‎to calm my nerves before surgery.

34
04:00.678 --> 04:02.638
‎How's Mr. Oh doing, by the way?

35
04:03.973 --> 04:05.558
‎VIP WARD

36
04:07.060 --> 04:08.519
‎Please calm down, Mr. Oh!

37
04:08.603 --> 04:09.937
‎Push a sedative now!

38
04:10.021 --> 04:11.314
‎You're in the hospital.

39
04:11.397 --> 04:14.650
‎You're in the hospital. You're safe.

40
04:14.734 --> 04:16.069
‎Please calm down. It's okay.

41
04:16.152 --> 04:17.904
‎Please, Mr. Oh. Please…

42
04:18.571 --> 04:19.822
‎Please calm down.

43
04:37.632 --> 04:39.550
‎What is he dreaming of

44
04:40.093 --> 04:43.096
‎that he can't sleep or stay awake?

45
04:43.846 --> 04:46.265
‎Did he get any real sleep over the years?

46
04:50.853 --> 04:52.480
‎So this is how it felt.

47
04:54.649 --> 04:55.650
‎What do you mean?

48
04:56.818 --> 04:57.944
‎Back then.

49
05:01.489 --> 05:02.448
‎You know when.

50
05:02.532 --> 05:04.575
‎-No! ‎-Su-jeong!

51
05:06.411 --> 05:08.538
‎-Su-jeong! ‎-Su-jeong!

52
05:09.080 --> 05:10.540
‎-It's okay, Su-jeong. ‎-Su-jeong.

53
05:10.623 --> 05:12.291
‎It's okay. We're at home.

54
05:24.595 --> 05:27.140
‎-All right, let's eat. ‎-Thank you.

55
05:27.807 --> 05:29.434
‎But I don't have an appetite--

56
05:29.517 --> 05:30.768
‎Thank you.

57
05:32.270 --> 05:34.272
‎Is this what Dr. Woo gave us?

58
05:37.024 --> 05:38.025
‎Here.

59
05:38.109 --> 05:41.112
‎This is how you enjoy marinated crab.

60
05:42.780 --> 05:44.866
‎-Go on, have a bite. ‎-Okay.

61
05:47.869 --> 05:49.203
‎It's really good.

62
05:50.913 --> 05:53.499
‎I wish Mr. Oh could eat this too.

63
05:53.583 --> 05:57.545
‎They may move him to a different floor ‎if his condition improves.

64
05:59.630 --> 06:00.840
‎But they talked about

65
06:01.674 --> 06:03.009
‎transferring him in the meeting.

66
06:04.385 --> 06:06.596
‎So he won't receive surgery?

67
06:06.679 --> 06:08.222
‎Does that mean the hospital is giving up?

68
06:08.306 --> 06:11.475
‎That's ridiculous. ‎Why should Mr. Oh be transferred?

69
06:11.559 --> 06:12.977
‎That other person should go.

70
06:13.060 --> 06:14.145
‎Thanks for the meal.

71
06:14.770 --> 06:16.355
‎Dr. Woo is coming.

72
06:17.064 --> 06:19.901
‎He wanted to come right away ‎but couldn't take time off.

73
06:20.985 --> 06:22.195
‎He wants us to discharge him.

74
06:24.197 --> 06:27.158
‎He says it's inhumane ‎and wants to take Mr. Oh home.

75
06:32.246 --> 06:34.248
‎-Apologize! ‎-Apologize!

76
06:34.332 --> 06:37.251
‎-Ji Du-seok must… ‎-Face justice!

77
06:37.335 --> 06:38.586
‎-Face justice! ‎-Face justice!

78
06:38.669 --> 06:40.922
‎-Ji Du-seok must… ‎-Apologize!

79
06:41.005 --> 06:43.007
‎-Apologize! ‎-Apologize!

80
06:43.090 --> 06:44.550
‎-Ji Du-seok must… ‎-Face justice!

81
06:44.634 --> 06:47.220
‎-Excuse me. ‎-Face justice!

82
06:47.720 --> 06:49.639
‎-This way, sir. ‎-Ji Du-seok must…

83
06:49.722 --> 06:51.724
‎-Apologize! ‎-Excuse me.

84
06:51.807 --> 06:53.726
‎-Ji Du-seok must… ‎-Pardon me.

85
06:57.021 --> 06:58.731
‎-Ms. Jang! ‎-Mr. Oh!

86
06:58.814 --> 07:00.900
‎Mr. Oh, can you hear me?

87
07:00.983 --> 07:01.984
‎Please.

88
07:03.110 --> 07:04.070
‎Please calm down.

89
07:04.904 --> 07:07.782
‎Sang-beom went to find his brother

90
07:07.865 --> 07:10.576
‎and somehow made it ‎to the provincial office.

91
07:11.619 --> 07:15.081
‎I guess Seung-beom, ‎his night school classmates,

92
07:15.164 --> 07:18.459
‎Seung-beom's cousin and uncle,

93
07:18.960 --> 07:22.004
‎and the diner owner were all there.

94
07:22.505 --> 07:25.383
‎How did that little kid ‎find his way here all by himself?

95
07:26.384 --> 07:27.969
‎-Let me look at you. ‎-He clawed his way

96
07:28.052 --> 07:29.804
‎through the chaos to find his brother.

97
07:37.895 --> 07:38.896
‎Eat up.

98
07:40.064 --> 07:42.733
‎He ate a rice ball with one hand

99
07:43.359 --> 07:46.362
‎-and held onto his brother with the other. ‎-Eat slowly.

100
07:46.445 --> 07:47.613
‎You're going to upset your stomach.

101
07:47.697 --> 07:50.783
‎Seung-beom tried to send Sang-beom home,

102
07:51.701 --> 07:56.038
‎but he dug in his heels ‎and refused to leave.

103
07:56.122 --> 07:58.791
‎Seung-beom, why do you need to be here?

104
07:59.500 --> 08:01.627
‎Mom's been looking for you everywhere.

105
08:02.670 --> 08:03.963
‎Let's go.

106
08:04.922 --> 08:06.090
‎Come on!

107
08:06.173 --> 08:07.216
‎Sang-beom.

108
08:08.301 --> 08:09.302
‎Listen, Sang-beom.

109
08:11.596 --> 08:13.055
‎Do you know what "conviction" means?

110
08:15.099 --> 08:15.933
‎No.

111
08:16.934 --> 08:18.060
‎I don't know.

112
08:22.106 --> 08:23.608
‎I'm glad you don't know.

113
08:25.526 --> 08:27.028
‎What a relief.

114
08:29.238 --> 08:30.114
‎Seung-beom.

115
08:30.698 --> 08:34.619
‎This is what college students ‎and politicians do.

116
08:36.704 --> 08:38.122
‎I know that much.

117
08:38.914 --> 08:42.001
‎It's not for people like us ‎with no education, no money,

118
08:42.084 --> 08:44.211
‎and no connections.

119
08:47.923 --> 08:48.924
‎I know.

120
08:50.760 --> 08:55.723
‎With no education, ‎no money, and no connections…

121
08:58.476 --> 09:02.271
‎I do wonder what we're doing here too.

122
09:10.404 --> 09:12.782
‎Please take good care of Sang-beom for me.

123
09:15.493 --> 09:16.869
‎-I'm staying. ‎-Sang-beom.

124
09:16.952 --> 09:19.664
‎-If you're staying, then so am I! ‎-Let go. Let's talk this out.

125
09:19.747 --> 09:22.333
‎-Hey, you two. Watch the gun! ‎-Sang-beom, stop!

126
09:22.416 --> 09:23.542
‎Sang-beom!

127
09:23.626 --> 09:25.252
‎-Hands off the gun! ‎-Hey!

128
09:25.336 --> 09:27.004
‎-Sang-beom! ‎-Darn it. Hey!

129
09:31.050 --> 09:31.967
‎It doesn't work?

130
09:45.272 --> 09:47.066
‎How will you fight them with these guns?

131
09:48.859 --> 09:50.069
‎How?

132
09:53.823 --> 09:54.824
‎I'm not going.

133
09:56.492 --> 09:59.495
‎If you won't go, neither will I!

134
10:00.621 --> 10:01.539
‎Sang-beom.

135
10:02.164 --> 10:03.541
‎Give it a rest, okay?

136
10:03.624 --> 10:07.253
‎Citizens, martial law troops ‎are invading right now.

137
10:07.336 --> 10:11.924
‎Our beloved brothers and sisters ‎are dying at their hands.

138
10:12.007 --> 10:14.343
‎He couldn't send him away at that point.

139
10:14.427 --> 10:16.679
‎We must fight them to the very end!

140
10:16.762 --> 10:18.556
‎That's when he saw it.

141
10:21.350 --> 10:22.435
‎He saw hell.

142
10:28.941 --> 10:31.152
‎-Mr. Oh! You're okay! ‎-Mr. Oh!

143
10:31.235 --> 10:32.945
‎Mr. Oh, look at me!

144
10:33.028 --> 10:35.406
‎-Just look at me and breathe. ‎-Calm down.

145
10:39.076 --> 10:40.286
‎Hey!

146
10:55.259 --> 10:56.343
‎Sang-beom!

147
10:58.679 --> 11:00.556
‎Sang-beom!

148
11:15.196 --> 11:18.908
‎Who the hell breaks hospital windows?

149
11:18.991 --> 11:21.994
‎They're flying drones ‎to livestream Ji Du-seok's room.

150
11:22.578 --> 11:25.164
‎I'm just relieved Dr. Gye ‎wasn't injured badly.

151
11:43.933 --> 11:45.309
‎You're doing it to die, right?

152
11:47.895 --> 11:48.979
‎The surgery, I mean.

153
11:49.647 --> 11:51.023
‎You want to die from it,

154
11:52.233 --> 11:53.067
‎not live.

155
11:55.069 --> 11:56.237
‎What?

156
11:56.320 --> 11:58.948
‎Sang-beom, what is she saying?

157
12:01.617 --> 12:04.745
‎"How on earth ‎can I get him to agree to surgery?"

158
12:05.329 --> 12:07.164
‎"He's only living to die."

159
12:09.583 --> 12:11.335
‎"How do I get him to the hospital?"

160
12:14.213 --> 12:15.297
‎I might fail.

161
12:18.884 --> 12:20.678
‎If I fail, you'll die.

162
12:23.639 --> 12:24.932
‎You gambled your life

163
12:25.683 --> 12:27.643
‎on a hopeless surgery.

164
12:27.726 --> 12:29.645
‎A life you couldn't end yourself.

165
12:30.229 --> 12:31.313
‎A life you're living…

166
12:33.065 --> 12:34.400
‎in someone else's place.

167
12:36.277 --> 12:38.237
‎And I also knew ‎you couldn't bear surviving

168
12:38.904 --> 12:41.407
‎without ever seeing your brother again

169
12:42.408 --> 12:45.578
‎once you learned the surgery ‎might be successful.

170
12:48.455 --> 12:51.333
‎Sang-beom, is that true?

171
12:52.042 --> 12:54.962
‎Did you agree to the surgery ‎so you could die?

172
12:55.546 --> 12:56.589
‎However,

173
12:57.172 --> 12:58.340
‎it's impossible.

174
12:58.424 --> 12:59.425
‎Not in my hands.

175
13:00.551 --> 13:02.678
‎I'm going to pull off this surgery.

176
13:03.846 --> 13:07.141
‎I won't let you run away ‎from a chance at life.

177
13:18.235 --> 13:19.528
‎You must have the surgery.

178
13:19.612 --> 13:22.323
‎Why would you do that? Why?

179
13:22.948 --> 13:24.074
‎You have to live.

180
13:24.158 --> 13:26.076
‎You have to try and live.

181
13:26.577 --> 13:28.203
‎You have to live!

182
13:28.287 --> 13:30.414
‎You have to try and live!

183
13:30.497 --> 13:31.749
‎You've got to!

184
13:49.516 --> 13:50.476
‎How did you know

185
13:51.477 --> 13:53.228
‎that he was only living to die?

186
13:54.021 --> 13:55.147
‎I knew the look.

187
13:57.358 --> 13:58.359
‎It said,

188
13:59.318 --> 14:02.696
‎"That person should've survived

189
14:03.697 --> 14:04.615
‎instead of me."

190
14:05.949 --> 14:07.910
‎Someone who has no choice ‎but to stay alive.

191
14:09.286 --> 14:11.497
‎Someone who's only alive and nothing more.

192
14:13.248 --> 14:14.875
‎Someone who punishes themselves

193
14:16.085 --> 14:17.670
‎just by staying alive.

194
14:21.715 --> 14:23.384
‎He had the look ‎only someone like that has.

195
14:26.387 --> 14:28.263
‎Well, I'm going to have ‎a great bowel movement tomorrow.

196
14:32.101 --> 14:32.935
‎Let's drop it.

197
14:34.687 --> 14:36.271
‎He doesn't want the surgery.

198
14:37.106 --> 14:39.274
‎And Dr. Woo is taking him back home.

199
14:40.609 --> 14:42.027
‎We did what we could.

200
14:43.696 --> 14:46.949
‎If this keeps up, ‎he'll break down completely.

201
14:51.120 --> 14:54.498
‎When I grabbed him on the rooftop, ‎I wondered,

202
14:55.457 --> 14:57.501
‎"Where else could he have gone?"

203
14:59.378 --> 15:01.588
‎"Even if the surgery is a success,

204
15:02.673 --> 15:05.968
‎could he really live a better life?"

205
15:07.136 --> 15:08.345
‎"And…

206
15:08.429 --> 15:11.598
‎what if he ends up on another rooftop?"

207
15:15.436 --> 15:17.521
‎Sorry, I'm really bringing us down.

208
15:18.272 --> 15:20.649
‎It's a long shot, ‎even if he wants to live.

209
15:21.650 --> 15:24.319
‎So how can we save someone ‎who's desperate to die?

210
15:28.657 --> 15:30.117
‎YOGURT DRINK

211
15:37.166 --> 15:39.376
‎You're always constipated. ‎I hope you get diarrhea.

212
15:39.460 --> 15:40.711
‎You little…

213
15:40.794 --> 15:43.213
‎-Don't say that in front of-- ‎-You've done it before.

214
15:50.054 --> 15:51.096
‎You saved a life.

215
16:05.861 --> 16:06.820
‎Dr. Gye.

216
16:08.989 --> 16:12.117
‎If the surgery goes well, ‎will it heal Mr. Oh's heart too?

217
16:13.285 --> 16:14.828
‎It will, right?

218
16:14.912 --> 16:16.080
‎You'll make it happen, right?

219
16:17.039 --> 16:19.083
‎I don't know anything.

220
16:19.166 --> 16:23.754
‎I have no idea what's best for him.

221
16:24.713 --> 16:25.714
‎I just…

222
16:26.256 --> 16:29.843
‎I just want him to sleep well, ‎if nothing else.

223
16:31.929 --> 16:33.931
‎But you know, don't you?

224
16:34.014 --> 16:35.933
‎There's a way, right?

225
18:34.259 --> 18:35.344
‎Think.

226
18:36.637 --> 18:38.388
‎You must think and find a way.

227
18:39.139 --> 18:42.100
‎If I can just operate on him…

228
18:43.143 --> 18:44.686
‎If I can just get it out…

229
18:46.021 --> 18:47.439
‎there's a chance.

230
18:48.357 --> 18:49.942
‎The doctor told the soldiers

231
18:50.025 --> 18:52.527
‎who were about to drag Mr. Oh away…

232
18:52.611 --> 18:53.570
‎GUNSHOT-INDUCED PENETRATING HEAD TRAUMA

233
18:54.196 --> 18:55.739
‎…that a bullet was lodged in his head.

234
18:57.241 --> 18:58.450
‎Push a sedative now!

235
18:58.533 --> 19:01.161
‎Asleep or awake, ‎you'd ask for your brother.

236
19:02.037 --> 19:05.290
‎You'd wake up in the middle of the night ‎crying and sobbing,

237
19:05.374 --> 19:08.126
‎"It's too heavy."

238
19:08.210 --> 19:10.629
‎You kept repeating that over and over.

239
19:17.511 --> 19:18.387
‎Look who it is.

240
19:21.181 --> 19:24.351
‎It's Dr. Gye, ‎Mr. Oh Sang-beom's primary surgeon.

241
19:24.434 --> 19:25.978
‎Clocking out?

242
19:26.061 --> 19:29.815
‎No point in monitoring a patient ‎who's being transferred, right?

243
19:30.399 --> 19:31.233
‎You didn't know?

244
19:32.150 --> 19:36.196
‎For someone who went on about ‎how he was your patient,

245
19:36.280 --> 19:37.489
‎you sure don't know much.

246
19:38.699 --> 19:39.825
‎There's no surgery.

247
19:39.908 --> 19:42.160
‎I think that's enough.

248
19:42.244 --> 19:43.870
‎What would a mere locum know?

249
19:46.290 --> 19:47.249
‎What?

250
19:47.332 --> 19:48.375
‎What is it?

251
19:49.001 --> 19:50.252
‎What are you up to now?

252
19:52.087 --> 19:52.921
‎Who are you?

253
19:53.005 --> 19:54.131
‎Seriously?

254
20:01.346 --> 20:02.764
‎-Hey. ‎-Hey!

255
20:03.557 --> 20:05.058
‎-Hey! ‎-Unbelievable.

256
20:05.142 --> 20:06.393
‎What's wrong with her?

257
20:06.476 --> 20:08.937
‎-She doesn't know me? ‎-Let's get you home, Mr. Oh.

258
20:09.021 --> 20:11.106
‎-She doesn't recognize me? ‎-Sir, please.

259
20:11.189 --> 20:13.942
‎-We met before. Hey! ‎-Sir…

260
20:14.026 --> 20:15.861
‎GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

261
20:24.161 --> 20:25.203
‎Go away.

262
20:27.539 --> 20:30.167
‎Macbeth…

263
20:31.084 --> 20:32.210
‎Macbeth…

264
20:33.337 --> 20:35.797
‎I'm sorry!

265
20:36.923 --> 20:38.967
‎What the heck? Jeez, that's cold.

266
20:39.051 --> 20:40.177
‎Theater club, right?

267
20:41.845 --> 20:42.763
‎Yes.

268
20:47.351 --> 20:48.185
‎Come in.

269
20:52.481 --> 20:55.359
‎DIRECTOR BU SEUNG-GWON

270
20:57.903 --> 20:58.779
‎Go on.

271
21:47.994 --> 21:51.373
‎Dr. Gye, Dr. Jo, Dr. Park,

272
21:51.456 --> 21:53.250
‎and Dr. Kim.

273
21:53.333 --> 21:56.753
‎I'll need an explanation for this.

274
21:56.837 --> 21:59.506
‎Ms. Jang requested that I come,

275
21:59.589 --> 22:01.299
‎so I obliged, but…

276
22:19.151 --> 22:20.694
‎Forty-six years ago,

277
22:21.570 --> 22:22.737
‎on that day,

278
22:22.821 --> 22:25.073
‎on that night, at that exact moment…

279
22:26.074 --> 22:27.284
‎We're here to show everyone

280
22:27.826 --> 22:30.495
‎what we imagine took place that day.

281
22:33.707 --> 22:36.877
‎Don't worry. Just take a seat and watch.

282
22:39.796 --> 22:41.798
‎They're reenacting that day.

283
22:44.467 --> 22:45.677
‎We found a room

284
22:46.428 --> 22:50.098
‎that most closely resembles ‎where it happened,

285
22:50.682 --> 22:52.893
‎including the windows, window size,

286
22:52.976 --> 22:54.853
‎ceiling height, and room width.

287
22:55.437 --> 22:58.106
‎According to witnesses, ‎at around 4 a.m. that day,

288
22:58.190 --> 23:01.651
‎a helicopter fired a machine gun ‎into the eighth-floor windows

289
23:01.735 --> 23:04.487
‎of the Gwangil Building.

290
23:05.739 --> 23:08.158
‎In the room was the 12-year-old Sang-beom.

291
23:12.787 --> 23:14.456
‎His 20-year-old brother, Seung-beom.

292
23:16.416 --> 23:17.542
‎The diner owner.

293
23:18.501 --> 23:19.920
‎The brothers' uncle.

294
23:24.424 --> 23:25.717
‎The brothers' uncle.

295
23:30.972 --> 23:31.932
‎The uncle, yes.

296
23:35.602 --> 23:36.436
‎And…

297
23:38.271 --> 23:40.190
‎Seung-beom's night school classmate.

298
23:41.566 --> 23:43.526
‎After the protest broadcast at dawn,

299
23:43.610 --> 23:48.031
‎everyone quickly entered the building ‎and settled in.

300
23:48.740 --> 23:52.118
‎But they didn't know ‎that a helicopter would be deployed

301
23:52.202 --> 23:54.371
‎or that a machine gun ‎would open fire on them.

302
24:02.045 --> 24:03.463
‎They heard the helicopter.

303
24:04.005 --> 24:06.716
‎They heard it getting closer and then…

304
24:08.134 --> 24:10.971
‎they saw it appear through the window.

305
24:11.846 --> 24:14.224
‎They tried to run,

306
24:15.850 --> 24:18.103
‎but a hail of bullets rained down on them.

307
24:18.186 --> 24:19.437
‎And those bullets…

308
24:37.497 --> 24:38.331
‎Seung-beom

309
24:39.082 --> 24:41.334
‎shielded his brother with his entire body.

310
24:43.420 --> 24:45.005
‎Sang-beom!

311
25:00.478 --> 25:03.398
‎It was impossible ‎for Seung-beom alone to protect him.

312
25:03.481 --> 25:05.025
‎But what if…

313
25:06.109 --> 25:07.485
‎What if it wasn't just him?

314
25:09.654 --> 25:10.530
‎Another person.

315
25:14.617 --> 25:15.452
‎And…

316
25:20.915 --> 25:22.083
‎another like this.

317
25:25.128 --> 25:27.630
‎And toward the diner owner ‎who was like a mother to them all…

318
25:30.675 --> 25:31.885
‎his classmate…

319
25:33.636 --> 25:35.722
‎his friend's uncle…

320
25:39.517 --> 25:40.727
‎and the young boy.

321
25:43.480 --> 25:44.397
‎Like this.

322
26:38.701 --> 26:39.702
‎Look.

323
27:40.555 --> 27:42.765
‎I just couldn't make sense of it.

324
27:44.017 --> 27:46.394
‎Even if it's outdated, it was still ‎a helicopter with a machine gun.

325
27:46.978 --> 27:49.355
‎How could a young child ‎have survived that?

326
27:51.149 --> 27:52.233
‎"It's too heavy."

327
27:53.151 --> 27:54.486
‎I heard

328
27:54.569 --> 27:56.779
‎you kept saying that ‎when you were in the hospital back then.

329
27:58.781 --> 27:59.699
‎So I thought

330
28:00.450 --> 28:01.743
‎maybe your brother

331
28:02.660 --> 28:05.163
‎wasn't the only one resting on top of you.

332
28:16.132 --> 28:18.218
‎Here, Sang-beom.

333
28:35.068 --> 28:36.361
‎Did you know?

334
28:38.821 --> 28:42.325
‎Did you know that was a possibility?

335
28:53.795 --> 28:54.963
‎It was…

336
29:01.928 --> 29:04.764
‎It was heavy.

337
29:13.815 --> 29:14.816
‎It was…

338
29:21.322 --> 29:24.659
‎too heavy.

339
29:32.542 --> 29:34.252
‎It was so…

340
29:45.889 --> 29:47.140
‎It was so…

341
29:56.065 --> 29:57.984
‎heavy.

342
30:14.208 --> 30:16.002
‎Mr. Oh.

343
30:16.794 --> 30:21.090
‎Is there a song or sound ‎you want to hear during the surgery?

344
30:22.091 --> 30:23.676
‎You'll be under anesthesia,

345
30:23.760 --> 30:27.305
‎but I thought it might ‎give you some comfort.

346
30:40.234 --> 30:42.362
‎TRÄUMEREI

347
30:43.363 --> 30:44.364
‎Okay.

348
30:56.334 --> 30:59.379
‎MY BROTHER LIKED THIS PIECE

349
31:21.859 --> 31:23.444
‎You only get to die once.

350
31:24.529 --> 31:25.738
‎So…

351
31:26.531 --> 31:27.615
‎save it for later.

352
31:28.491 --> 31:29.784
‎Put it off until tomorrow

353
31:29.867 --> 31:32.245
‎and then the next day.

354
31:33.329 --> 31:34.539
‎Keep putting it off.

355
31:38.501 --> 31:39.877
‎I'll make sure you get home.

356
31:40.420 --> 31:41.629
‎With your brother.

357
31:43.339 --> 31:44.340
‎No matter what.

358
31:47.051 --> 31:48.219
‎Don't worry.

359
31:48.302 --> 31:49.512
‎I…

360
31:51.014 --> 31:52.223
‎don't ever fail.

361
32:12.326 --> 32:15.663
‎His vitals are stable, ‎and he's in good condition.

362
32:37.060 --> 32:38.144
‎You think Dr. Gye can do this?

363
33:07.632 --> 33:08.925
‎Mr. Oh Sang-beom.

364
33:09.008 --> 33:11.928
‎Right-sided neuroendoscopic ‎foreign body removal.

365
33:12.512 --> 33:13.679
‎Let's begin.

366
33:44.585 --> 33:49.924
‎MAY 18 OLD CEMETERY

367
34:27.128 --> 34:28.045
‎Sheath.

368
34:28.129 --> 34:30.673
‎SHEATH: A SHORT TUBE THAT FACILITATES ‎VASCULAR ACCESS FOR CATHETERS &amp; GUIDEWIRES

369
34:35.761 --> 34:36.846
‎Endoscope.

370
34:41.392 --> 34:46.522
‎-But one night, they got caught in a storm ‎-But one night, they got caught in a storm

371
34:46.606 --> 34:49.066
‎-And everyone vanished… ‎-And everyone vanished…

372
35:02.246 --> 35:03.372
‎Cheers.

373
35:38.574 --> 35:39.533
‎There it is.

374
35:48.000 --> 35:49.001
‎Sang-beom.

375
35:50.878 --> 35:51.879
‎Sang-beom.

376
35:54.090 --> 35:55.258
‎Get up.

377
35:57.510 --> 35:58.386
‎Eat first, then sleep.

378
36:01.180 --> 36:02.348
‎Get your strength back first.

379
36:11.899 --> 36:12.858
‎Biopsy forceps.

380
36:12.942 --> 36:16.445
‎BIOPSY FORCEPS: ENDOSCOPIC FORCEPS ‎USED TO COLLECT TISSUE SAMPLES FOR BIOPSY

381
36:25.705 --> 36:28.666
‎When I ask for biopsy forceps, ‎leave the OR.

382
36:28.749 --> 36:30.126
‎What? But I need to close--

383
36:30.209 --> 36:31.377
‎Wait at the end of the hallway.

384
36:33.421 --> 36:34.255
‎Okay.

385
36:37.508 --> 36:38.676
‎No questions?

386
36:38.759 --> 36:40.177
‎No. Not a single one.

387
36:40.261 --> 36:42.680
‎I'll leave and wait ‎at the end of the hallway.

388
36:45.391 --> 36:46.392
‎I'll do as you say.

389
37:16.589 --> 37:17.590
‎Sang-beom.

390
37:19.633 --> 37:20.760
‎Take care of yourself.

391
37:22.887 --> 37:24.013
‎Eat well…

392
37:28.601 --> 37:29.727
‎and sleep well, okay?

393
37:34.648 --> 37:35.900
‎Live well, just like that.

394
39:08.492 --> 39:09.326
‎What's that?

395
39:09.410 --> 39:10.661
‎Is that the bullet?

396
39:10.744 --> 39:12.079
‎-Did you get a good look? ‎-Not really.

397
39:12.163 --> 39:13.247
‎What is it?

398
39:24.091 --> 39:26.218
‎-What's going on? ‎-Excuse me.

399
39:27.636 --> 39:28.512
‎Is that it?

400
39:29.305 --> 39:30.723
‎Is that a bullet?

401
39:31.640 --> 39:32.516
‎Well…

402
39:32.600 --> 39:34.518
‎I think it is.

403
39:34.602 --> 39:35.644
‎But…

404
39:35.728 --> 39:36.729
‎-I can't see it. ‎-What?

405
39:36.812 --> 39:37.855
‎Is that a bullet?

406
40:38.374 --> 40:40.209
‎OPERATING ROOM

407
40:47.132 --> 40:48.884
‎-Hey, was it really a bullet? ‎-Dr. Gye.

408
40:48.968 --> 40:50.886
‎The color was off. What was it?

409
40:52.054 --> 40:53.222
‎I asked you a question!

410
40:53.305 --> 40:55.015
‎Dr. Gye, just hand it over.

411
40:55.099 --> 40:57.017
‎Was it really a bullet?

412
40:57.101 --> 40:59.186
‎Just show us already!

413
41:12.157 --> 41:13.158
‎Park Tae-gyeong.

414
41:13.242 --> 41:14.743
‎Yes, Dr. Gye!

415
41:14.827 --> 41:15.953
‎I'm right here!

416
41:19.123 --> 41:20.082
‎Hey!

417
41:28.007 --> 41:29.258
‎-Wait… ‎-Run.

418
41:30.426 --> 41:31.969
‎-Got it! ‎-Dr. Gye, what the hell?

419
41:32.052 --> 41:33.178
‎Have you lost your mind?

420
41:35.264 --> 41:36.765
‎Hey! Park Tae-gyeong!

421
41:44.898 --> 41:47.359
‎I knew you'd stay behind.

422
41:47.901 --> 41:49.403
‎I allowed the surgery

423
41:49.486 --> 41:51.822
‎under the premise that it was a bullet.

424
41:53.407 --> 41:56.452
‎I never said it was a bullet.

425
42:00.414 --> 42:01.457
‎Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

426
42:06.462 --> 42:09.006
‎There's another specimen container

427
42:09.089 --> 42:11.342
‎in your pocket right now.

428
42:11.425 --> 42:13.427
‎Is it what I think it is?

429
42:14.678 --> 42:16.180
‎What do you think it is?

430
42:18.057 --> 42:19.224
‎A bone fragment.

431
42:24.688 --> 42:28.525
‎Everyone will soon find out ‎about your lie, Dr. Gye.

432
42:38.786 --> 42:41.163
‎You'll find Ms. Jang at Gate 3.

433
42:42.498 --> 42:44.333
‎A bribe? Well, who'd have thought?

434
42:48.087 --> 42:49.004
‎You're not changing?

435
42:54.843 --> 42:57.012
‎Everyone looks pretty angry.

436
42:57.096 --> 42:58.222
‎Is that her?

437
42:58.305 --> 42:59.890
‎-Dr. Gye. ‎-It is!

438
42:59.973 --> 43:01.642
‎-You know what you're doing right now? ‎-Hey!

439
43:01.725 --> 43:02.601
‎Come here!

440
43:03.227 --> 43:04.770
‎-Wasting time? ‎-Get over here!

441
43:04.853 --> 43:07.064
‎No, you're making yourself available ‎to be on call.

442
43:07.147 --> 43:09.441
‎Never thought I'd see you ‎volunteer to be on call.

443
43:10.734 --> 43:13.112
‎-Hey! ‎-Go grab her right now!

444
43:13.195 --> 43:14.321
‎Goodness gracious.

445
43:16.573 --> 43:17.491
‎Dr. Jo.

446
43:19.243 --> 43:20.327
‎Guess you're a good runner.

447
43:20.994 --> 43:23.789
‎You and I have been ‎running a lot recently.

448
43:23.872 --> 43:24.873
‎Tell me about it.

449
43:28.210 --> 43:29.378
‎Is it that car?

450
43:32.881 --> 43:34.258
‎-Hold on. ‎-The window, please.

451
43:35.342 --> 43:36.510
‎Oh, the window…

452
43:37.803 --> 43:39.096
‎Wait.

453
43:39.179 --> 43:40.597
‎-Here. ‎-Through here?

454
43:40.681 --> 43:42.683
‎Got it. Thank you both!

455
43:42.766 --> 43:44.476
‎-Take care. ‎-Thank you.

456
43:46.812 --> 43:48.689
‎-Goodness. ‎-Hello.

457
43:48.772 --> 43:49.773
‎Hello.

458
43:49.857 --> 43:53.068
‎Gye Su-jeong, you'd better make a fortune.

459
43:53.152 --> 43:55.028
‎I'll make you pay for this.

460
43:55.112 --> 43:56.321
‎-Goodbye then. ‎-Goodbye.

461
43:58.991 --> 44:00.325
‎Think she'll be okay?

462
44:03.328 --> 44:05.956
‎It's a miracle they've been okay so far.

463
44:15.382 --> 44:17.176
‎No wonder they all lost their heads.

464
44:17.259 --> 44:19.052
‎It's completely empty.

465
44:19.136 --> 44:20.929
‎It's not empty.

466
44:21.597 --> 44:22.431
‎It's full.

467
44:22.514 --> 44:23.515
‎What?

468
44:24.683 --> 44:25.893
‎Dedication.

469
44:25.976 --> 44:28.729
‎It's filled with Dr. Gye's dedication ‎to her patients.

470
44:28.812 --> 44:29.688
‎And sincerity.

471
44:29.772 --> 44:32.983
‎Have you been talking to Dr. Kim?

472
44:33.066 --> 44:35.360
‎Comments like that are his specialty.

473
44:35.444 --> 44:36.820
‎Don't get too close to him.

474
44:36.904 --> 44:38.781
‎She called me by name for the first time.

475
44:38.864 --> 44:40.657
‎She shouted my name super loud…

476
44:40.741 --> 44:41.784
‎Park Tae-gyeong!

477
44:42.618 --> 44:43.994
‎Buzzkill Won-jin!

478
44:44.077 --> 44:45.329
‎What the heck? Why is he here?

479
44:45.412 --> 44:47.206
‎He said post-show ‎wrap-up parties are a must

480
44:47.289 --> 44:49.208
‎-and asked where we're going. ‎-Forget it.

481
44:49.291 --> 44:50.459
‎Where are you going?

482
44:50.542 --> 44:52.336
‎-Wrap-up party, right? ‎-Wait, Dr. Kim.

483
44:52.419 --> 44:54.546
‎-Right? Take me with you. ‎-No, it's not like that.

484
44:54.630 --> 44:57.049
‎-Dr. Kim, where are you going? ‎-Stop following me!

485
45:08.435 --> 45:10.521
‎The results will be out soon.

486
45:10.604 --> 45:12.689
‎If you're wrong, ‎I'm not feeding you for two days.

487
45:13.190 --> 45:14.566
‎And no allowance either.

488
45:23.450 --> 45:25.118
‎Guess he's not dreaming tonight.

489
45:30.874 --> 45:32.960
‎GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

490
45:36.380 --> 45:39.383
‎I still can't believe it wasn't a bullet.

491
45:39.466 --> 45:41.927
‎Should we really be holding ‎a press conference?

492
45:42.010 --> 45:45.138
‎They say this will be even more tragic.

493
45:45.222 --> 45:47.140
‎-Who said that? ‎-Those guys.

494
45:47.808 --> 45:49.434
‎What about that person upstairs?

495
45:50.143 --> 45:51.562
‎He's still here.

496
46:01.613 --> 46:02.614
‎Here.

497
46:03.574 --> 46:06.910
‎I got this for you ‎at a nearby shop yesterday.

498
46:18.380 --> 46:20.966
‎I'm glad you made it through.

499
46:22.551 --> 46:24.511
‎After the press conference,

500
46:25.762 --> 46:28.140
‎we're heading home, okay?

501
47:00.672 --> 47:01.923
‎Is he gone now?

502
47:15.520 --> 47:18.273
‎I'm glad we were able to ‎hold this press conference.

503
47:20.108 --> 47:22.819
‎There's really no point ‎if it's not a bullet.

504
47:22.903 --> 47:24.988
‎Makes you wonder why we did any of this.

505
47:25.072 --> 47:29.743
‎His X-rays would've shown it ‎when he came in to get examined.

506
47:29.826 --> 47:30.744
‎Why didn't she tell us?

507
47:30.827 --> 47:33.622
‎Because she wanted to operate!

508
47:33.705 --> 47:36.875
‎That Gye Su-jeong or whatever ‎is obsessed with performing surgery.

509
47:36.958 --> 47:40.087
‎I think Dr. Gye's actions ‎were along the same lines

510
47:40.170 --> 47:43.590
‎as those of the doctors from back then.

511
47:45.509 --> 47:46.635
‎What did you say?

512
47:47.511 --> 47:50.097
‎-Are you taking her side? ‎-Of course not.

513
47:50.180 --> 47:52.015
‎She's in the wrong. She lied, after all.

514
47:52.099 --> 47:55.769
‎What am I supposed to say ‎at the press conference later?

515
47:55.852 --> 47:57.688
‎I'm going to lose face!

516
47:57.771 --> 47:58.855
‎If they'd known

517
47:58.939 --> 48:02.109
‎it was a bone fragment and not a bullet,

518
48:03.485 --> 48:05.821
‎would those blowhards ‎have funded his surgery?

519
48:07.239 --> 48:10.909
‎Sir, I'm not the slightest bit interested

520
48:10.992 --> 48:12.369
‎in shaping or running the world.

521
48:13.370 --> 48:15.580
‎I'm not someone who says "yes"

522
48:16.373 --> 48:17.249
‎or "no."

523
48:18.250 --> 48:19.251
‎All I am

524
48:20.460 --> 48:21.294
‎is someone…

525
48:22.796 --> 48:24.631
‎who asks, "Why?"

526
48:26.299 --> 48:27.342
‎"Why?"

527
48:30.303 --> 48:31.388
‎"Why?"

528
48:35.600 --> 48:36.435
‎Yes?

529
48:38.186 --> 48:39.813
‎Huh? What do you mean?

530
48:40.397 --> 48:42.733
‎Mr. Oh Sang-beom has disappeared?

531
48:45.527 --> 48:47.487
‎My word. Look at these potatoes.

532
48:48.113 --> 48:51.783
‎Back in North Korea, ‎potatoes kept me alive.

533
48:52.909 --> 48:54.453
‎It's Dr. Woo.

534
48:55.370 --> 48:56.496
‎Hello, Dr. Woo.

535
48:57.247 --> 48:59.875
‎-Stop that. ‎-I've been meaning to call you.

536
49:01.251 --> 49:02.461
‎What?

537
49:02.544 --> 49:03.837
‎I mean,

538
49:03.920 --> 49:06.214
‎I only took a quick bathroom break.

539
49:06.298 --> 49:07.758
‎-Dr. Gye. ‎-No, he's not here.

540
49:08.341 --> 49:10.051
‎He's not in his room.

541
49:12.554 --> 49:15.348
‎THANK YOU FOR EVERYTHING ‎I'M SORRY

542
49:38.330 --> 49:39.372
‎Dr. Gye.

543
49:40.540 --> 49:42.751
‎He's not on the rooftop, ‎which is a relief.

544
49:43.335 --> 49:44.336
‎A huge relief.

545
49:44.419 --> 49:46.379
‎I checked the CCTVs, but found nothing.

546
49:46.922 --> 49:48.423
‎I think he's still in the hospital.

547
49:50.217 --> 49:51.676
‎GWANGJU UPRISING VICTIM SURGERY RESULTS

548
49:51.760 --> 49:55.472
‎The tragedy that took place in Gwangju ‎is a tragedy for us all.

549
49:55.555 --> 49:59.017
‎The pain felt in Gwangju ‎is a pain we all share.

550
49:59.100 --> 50:02.979
‎The bone fragment recovered during surgery

551
50:04.064 --> 50:07.359
‎reveals the details of that tragedy.

552
50:08.151 --> 50:09.277
‎The bullet's path.

553
50:09.861 --> 50:12.489
‎The shattered fragments of grief ‎lodged deep within.

554
50:12.989 --> 50:14.074
‎Can we really

555
50:14.157 --> 50:16.868
‎-turn our backs on this? ‎-He sure does have a silver tongue.

556
50:17.452 --> 50:20.080
‎He commands the room well.

557
50:20.163 --> 50:21.623
‎This turned out for the better.

558
50:21.706 --> 50:24.626
‎If Mr. Oh were here, ‎he couldn't go all out that way.

559
50:25.126 --> 50:26.795
‎The focus wouldn't have been ‎on the mayor either.

560
50:26.878 --> 50:28.797
‎We must not let a tragedy like this…

561
50:28.880 --> 50:30.549
‎Director, about the statement ‎we put together earlier.

562
50:31.842 --> 50:33.093
‎I trust that you'll stick to it.

563
50:43.186 --> 50:44.229
‎Get in!

564
50:44.312 --> 50:46.940
‎He's not from around here, ‎so he couldn't have gotten far.

565
50:47.023 --> 50:48.817
‎-Get in. ‎-Oh, I…

566
50:48.900 --> 50:50.944
‎I'll take my car. It's safer than…

567
50:51.027 --> 50:52.487
‎-Just get in. ‎-But…

568
50:52.571 --> 50:54.823
‎-Hurry up. ‎-Wait, Ms. Jang, I…

569
50:57.075 --> 50:58.285
‎-Seat belts! ‎-Okay.

570
51:02.080 --> 51:05.166
‎Next, Director Bu Seung-gwon

571
51:05.250 --> 51:07.252
‎will take questions.

572
51:08.545 --> 51:10.338
‎So they take all the credit

573
51:10.422 --> 51:12.299
‎and leave the director to take the blame?

574
51:12.382 --> 51:13.425
‎Be quiet.

575
51:13.508 --> 51:16.303
‎Why not do everything themselves ‎instead of involving the director?

576
51:16.386 --> 51:19.306
‎He just agreed to it ‎for the future of this hospital.

577
51:19.389 --> 51:22.976
‎I'd like to thank all the reporters ‎who have joined us today.

578
51:23.518 --> 51:26.980
‎I'm Director Bu Seung-gwon ‎of Guseo University Medical Center.

579
51:27.063 --> 51:28.440
‎I'll take questions now.

580
51:30.358 --> 51:32.193
‎Why isn't Mr. Oh Sang-beom in attendance?

581
51:32.277 --> 51:35.739
‎He hasn't recovered yet ‎and needs more rest.

582
51:38.950 --> 51:42.203
‎Test results would've shown ‎it wasn't a bullet,

583
51:42.287 --> 51:43.663
‎so why was the surgery performed?

584
51:44.247 --> 51:48.460
‎Word is that the original plan was ‎to transfer him because of Mr. Ji Du-seok.

585
52:19.157 --> 52:20.742
‎OBOK NOODLES

586
52:20.825 --> 52:21.660
‎Please answer us.

587
52:21.743 --> 52:23.119
‎Why did you operate on him?

588
52:23.828 --> 52:26.456
‎X-rays did indeed show

589
52:27.040 --> 52:31.169
‎it was a bone fragment ‎rather than a bullet.

590
52:31.711 --> 52:35.924
‎However, we couldn't simply ignore

591
52:36.007 --> 52:39.427
‎an issue that has disrupted ‎the patient's life.

592
52:40.011 --> 52:43.974
‎To be honest, ‎it was an extremely risky surgery.

593
52:44.557 --> 52:48.937
‎But our hospital's exceptional doctors,

594
52:49.020 --> 52:51.648
‎alongside our esteemed contributors, ‎Mayor Im Ho-seok,

595
52:52.190 --> 52:55.527
‎Chairman Kim Chang-su ‎of the Medical Association,

596
52:55.610 --> 52:59.990
‎and Chairman Gu Bon-pyeong ‎of Guseo Foundation,

597
53:00.824 --> 53:02.075
‎were determined.

598
53:03.952 --> 53:06.079
‎Are you really not going to accept these?

599
53:06.162 --> 53:07.872
‎Take them away before I change my mind.

600
53:08.373 --> 53:11.334
‎Don't use the lack of a bullet ‎as an excuse

601
53:11.418 --> 53:14.587
‎to withdraw funding for the surgery ‎and saddle Mr. Oh

602
53:15.839 --> 53:16.881
‎with huge medical bills.

603
53:20.051 --> 53:21.052
‎May I ask why?

604
53:23.304 --> 53:25.724
‎There's this word, "neujagu," ‎in the Jeolla dialect.

605
53:26.641 --> 53:28.977
‎I don't want people to say ‎that I have no ‎neujagu‎.

606
53:29.686 --> 53:30.770
‎"Neujagu"?

607
53:31.396 --> 53:32.439
‎"Basic decency"?

608
53:34.107 --> 53:35.066
‎Goodbye.

609
53:36.026 --> 53:37.527
‎Damn it!

610
53:37.610 --> 53:40.196
‎I really wanted to get a new car.

611
53:43.408 --> 53:44.534
‎Where is it?

612
53:45.952 --> 53:47.078
‎Here.

613
53:47.162 --> 53:50.331
‎-Isn't that Mr. Oh's bone fragment-- ‎-No.

614
53:50.415 --> 53:51.332
‎What?

615
53:51.875 --> 53:53.543
‎It's not Mr. Oh's.

616
53:56.755 --> 53:59.049
‎-Hey, there's Mr. Oh! ‎-Where?

617
54:00.592 --> 54:02.093
‎He went into that back alley.

618
54:03.053 --> 54:06.723
‎Mr. Oh Sang-beom ‎was 12 years old at the time.

619
54:07.307 --> 54:10.351
‎When martial law troops ‎tried to take him away again,

620
54:10.435 --> 54:12.228
‎I imagine the primary attending

621
54:12.812 --> 54:16.024
‎told him a white lie

622
54:16.107 --> 54:17.275
‎at the time.

623
54:18.151 --> 54:21.905
‎And when his records ‎were burned in a fire,

624
54:21.988 --> 54:23.490
‎that white lie became a fact.

625
54:25.492 --> 54:29.329
‎We took in both ‎Mr. Oh Sang-beom and Mr. Ji Du-seok

626
54:29.412 --> 54:31.831
‎because they were patients.

627
54:32.499 --> 54:35.960
‎We never once considered ‎transferring either of them.

628
54:36.544 --> 54:38.379
‎Like the doctors back then,

629
54:38.463 --> 54:40.090
‎everyone in our hospital

630
54:41.382 --> 54:42.926
‎shares the same dedication

631
54:43.718 --> 54:46.262
‎to uphold our obligations with…

632
54:47.931 --> 54:51.226
‎TO UPHOLD OUR OBLIGATIONS ‎WITH A "WHITE-COAT" SENSE OF DUTY

633
54:52.936 --> 54:54.104
‎With a white-coat…

634
54:58.399 --> 55:01.152
‎-With a white-coat sense of duty-- ‎-Code blue.

635
55:01.236 --> 55:04.155
‎-"Code blue"? ‎-Third floor, VIP ward, Room 5.

636
55:04.239 --> 55:07.784
‎Cardiology and cardiothoracic surgery. ‎Code blue.

637
55:07.867 --> 55:10.161
‎Third floor, VIP ward, Room 5.

638
55:10.245 --> 55:12.247
‎-Cardiology and cardiothoracic surgery. ‎-Room 5?

639
55:13.915 --> 55:14.749
‎Ji Du-seok?

640
55:14.833 --> 55:16.584
‎-Ji Du-seok? ‎-Ji Du-seok?

641
55:16.668 --> 55:19.045
‎The code blue is for Ji Du-seok! ‎It's for Ji Du-seok!

642
55:19.129 --> 55:20.922
‎Is this about former President Ji Du-seok?

643
55:21.005 --> 55:23.341
‎Excuse me, I haven't finished--

644
55:23.424 --> 55:25.176
‎Doesn't code blue mean cardiac arrest?

645
55:25.260 --> 55:26.761
‎Were there issues ‎with the initial response?

646
55:26.845 --> 55:28.429
‎-I'll respond after I-- ‎-Is it Mr. Ji Du-seok?

647
55:28.513 --> 55:30.515
‎Was he really conscious during transport?

648
55:30.598 --> 55:31.641
‎What was the cause?

649
55:31.724 --> 55:33.434
‎-We should go, Director. ‎-What was his status at the time?

650
55:33.518 --> 55:34.853
‎When did his condition worsen?

651
55:34.936 --> 55:37.647
‎-I'll update you with details soon. ‎-My source in another hospital…

652
55:37.730 --> 55:39.983
‎-I'll hold another briefing for this. ‎-What's the cause?

653
55:40.066 --> 55:41.276
‎Please respond!

654
55:41.359 --> 55:43.862
‎-Wait! Are you just leaving? ‎-Did he take a turn for the worse?

655
55:43.945 --> 55:46.072
‎-Please give us a comment! ‎-Please respond!

656
55:47.574 --> 55:48.825
‎Shouldn't you get back?

657
55:48.908 --> 55:50.702
‎He's not my patient.

658
55:56.708 --> 55:58.543
‎He went inside a karaoke bar.

659
55:59.294 --> 56:01.296
‎He bought something ‎from a convenience store.

660
56:01.379 --> 56:03.089
‎I don't know why, ‎but the black plastic bag

661
56:03.173 --> 56:04.549
‎is giving me a bad feeling.

662
56:23.484 --> 56:25.445
‎So this is where he is!

663
56:26.696 --> 56:28.364
‎There you are!

664
56:28.907 --> 56:31.409
‎You came to a fun place. Hey, get in here.

665
56:31.993 --> 56:33.620
‎All right, choose a song.

666
56:33.703 --> 56:35.663
‎I'll go ahead and kick us off.

667
56:35.747 --> 56:37.207
‎You can choose after my turn.

668
56:37.290 --> 56:38.708
‎All right, here we go.

669
56:39.918 --> 56:44.172
‎Okay, 0-4-5-0-1-7. Start.

670
56:53.097 --> 56:54.474
‎This just in.

671
56:54.557 --> 56:57.936
‎At 11:45 a.m., former President Ji Du-seok

672
56:58.019 --> 57:00.438
‎passed away at the age of 91.

673
57:01.022 --> 57:05.193
‎Former President Ji, ‎who has seen a sharp decline in health,

674
57:05.276 --> 57:08.321
‎took a sudden turn for the worse ‎while hospitalized

675
57:08.905 --> 57:11.991
‎and subsequently suffered cardiac arrest.

676
57:12.533 --> 57:15.245
‎The medical community is…

677
57:15.328 --> 57:20.708
‎A rock island where the waves crash

678
57:21.376 --> 57:25.922
‎To this place that used to be deserted

679
57:26.798 --> 57:32.595
‎People around the world

680
57:34.180 --> 57:38.351
‎Gathered one by one

681
57:39.936 --> 57:45.942
‎But one night, they got caught in a storm

682
57:47.193 --> 57:51.072
‎And everyone vanished…

683
57:53.116 --> 57:55.368
‎We had to wait for the DNA test results,

684
57:55.451 --> 57:56.995
‎so I couldn't tell you earlier.

685
58:03.751 --> 58:05.169
‎This is your brother's bone fragment.

686
58:13.303 --> 58:16.431
‎All this time, what was inside your head

687
58:17.640 --> 58:18.766
‎was your brother.

688
58:20.018 --> 58:21.060
‎He was…

689
58:21.894 --> 58:22.729
‎always with you.

690
58:30.028 --> 58:30.987
‎Seung-beom.

691
58:32.947 --> 58:33.948
‎Come on.

692
58:36.284 --> 58:37.285
‎Let's…

693
58:41.706 --> 58:42.707
‎go home.

694
59:23.164 --> 59:26.918
‎New evidence has emerged ‎proving that helicopter gunfire took place

695
59:27.001 --> 59:29.295
‎during the Gwangju Democratic Uprising.

696
59:29.379 --> 59:30.755
‎On the last day of the uprising,

697
59:30.838 --> 59:33.841
‎witnesses claimed the Gwangil Building ‎was targeted from the air.

698
59:33.925 --> 59:36.052
‎Hundreds of bullet holes were found

699
59:36.135 --> 59:38.388
‎in a room on the eighth floor ‎of that very building.

700
59:39.097 --> 59:40.431
‎Martial law troops used cement

701
59:40.515 --> 59:41.933
‎-to cover every bullet hole ‎-Mommy!

702
59:42.016 --> 59:44.519
‎and signs of armed suppression,

703
59:44.602 --> 59:47.563
‎making evidence extremely hard to find.

704
59:48.147 --> 59:51.109
‎This room, however, ‎remained largely untouched

705
59:51.192 --> 59:53.778
‎because it served as a storage room ‎after the uprising.

706
59:54.278 --> 59:56.531
‎-Families of the victims and NGOs ‎-Dr. Gye, over here.

707
59:56.614 --> 59:58.574
‎are demanding that the government ‎conduct further investigation.

708
59:58.658 --> 01:00:00.743
‎The May 18 Truth Commission

709
01:00:00.827 --> 01:00:03.913
‎also announced a probe ‎comparing the bullet holes

710
01:00:03.996 --> 01:00:05.748
‎with the martial law command's ‎operational logs.

711
01:00:06.624 --> 01:00:09.877
‎This just in. The government ‎is expanding the medical school quota.

712
01:00:09.961 --> 01:00:12.046
‎-It's official? ‎-They're pushing ahead with it?

713
01:00:12.130 --> 01:00:13.715
‎This isn't the time for that.

714
01:00:13.798 --> 01:00:16.300
‎Enrollment will increase ‎by more than 2,000 students

715
01:00:16.384 --> 01:00:18.010
‎-‎starting next year. ‎-Let's go.

716
01:00:18.094 --> 01:00:20.138
‎The Medical Association ‎will hold an emergency meeting.

717
01:00:20.221 --> 01:00:21.472
‎You bet they will.

718
01:00:21.556 --> 01:00:22.724
‎GOVERNMENT TO INCREASE ‎MED SCHOOL QUOTA BY 2,000

719
01:00:22.807 --> 01:00:25.393
‎This is the first time ‎the quota has been increased

720
01:00:25.476 --> 01:00:27.270
‎after being rejected ‎over the past 17 years…

721
01:00:28.438 --> 01:00:31.065
‎The move was pushed through ‎despite heavy opposition

722
01:00:31.149 --> 01:00:32.734
‎from the medical community.

723
01:00:33.359 --> 01:00:36.863
‎The Korean Medical Association protested, ‎citing risks of lower service quality

724
01:00:36.946 --> 01:00:39.574
‎-and excessive competition. ‎-You can have it all.

725
01:00:39.657 --> 01:00:43.369
‎University hospitals nationwide ‎echoed their concern.

726
01:00:44.120 --> 01:00:47.331
‎The Korean Intern Resident Association ‎and the Korean Medical Association

727
01:00:47.415 --> 01:00:48.791
‎have warned of a nationwide strike…

728
01:00:48.875 --> 01:00:51.586
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

729
01:01:31.542 --> 01:01:33.628
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

730
01:01:34.253 --> 01:01:38.090
‎All residents and interns ‎will stop working and leave the hospital.

731
01:01:38.174 --> 01:01:40.051
‎It's as if someone placed a huge rock

732
01:01:40.134 --> 01:01:41.886
‎on that 10-year-old's stomach.

733
01:01:41.969 --> 01:01:44.639
‎If you won't remove it, ‎at least look the other way.

734
01:01:44.722 --> 01:01:48.100
‎How can you call your colleagues traitors ‎for choosing to stay and treat patients?

735
01:01:48.184 --> 01:01:49.936
‎You call yourselves doctors?

736
01:01:50.019 --> 01:01:53.397
‎They're taking legal action ‎against doctors who leave their posts.

737
01:01:53.481 --> 01:01:56.025
‎It's because we're doctors ‎that we can't look the other way!

738
01:01:56.818 --> 01:01:58.778
‎If you're a doctor, scrub in with me.

739
01:01:59.737 --> 01:02:04.742
‎Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim
